course: dictionary
lesson: 11602
title: Applaud: clapping and praise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To applaud means to clap your hands to show you liked something, such as a show, a speech or a performance. «The audience applauded when the children finished their play.» The clapping shows that the audience enjoyed it.
explain: Applaud can also mean to praise someone for doing something right. «The head teacher applauded the class for their kindness.» Nobody has to clap here. The word shows that the head teacher approved of what the class did.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Who is watching? What just happened? Words like play, speech, kind or brave tell you that applaud means clapping or praising. Then swap your meaning into the sentence: if «The audience clapped when the children finished their play» still makes sense, you are right.
fact: «Applaud» is a verb, so it shows an action. Its forms are applaud, applauds, applauded and applauding.
fact: «Applaud» means to clap your hands to show you liked a show, a speech or a performance.
fact: «Applaud» can also mean to praise someone or say they did the right thing.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «applaud loudly», «applaud the decision» and «stand and applaud».
fact: You can read a whole text well without knowing every word; use the clues around the word to work out its meaning.
exercise: «The crowd began to applaud when the magician finished his trick.» What does applaud mean here? | To run away quickly | To fall asleep | To sing a sad song | *To clap hands to show they liked it
exercise: «The class applauded Ruby for helping a new pupil.» Why did the class applaud? | They were bored | They were angry with her | *They thought her kind act was good | They wanted an early lunch
exercise: Find and copy one word that is a form of applaud in this sentence: «The people applauded loudly, and the singer smiled.» | *applauded | people | smiled | singer
test: Which sentence uses applaud to mean praise? | The dog barked at the postman | The crowd applauded the lovely play | *The head teacher applauded the class for their honesty | We ate our lunch in the hall
test: Which word is the past form of applaud? | applauding | *applauded | applauds | applause
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The judges applauded the brave firefighter»? | To ignore him completely | *To praise him and clap for him | To look at the sky | To leave the room quietly
